      "summaries": {
        "en": "GenericAgent is a lightweight Python framework that enables AI agents to autonomously control computer systems through browser and desktop automation, solving the challenge of high computational costs in traditional agent systems. Its core innovation is a self-evolving skill tree that starts from a 3.3K-line seed and expands capabilities while reducing token consumption by 6x through efficient memory management. Developers can use it to build agents for tasks like automated testing, data collection, or workflow automation by integrating with models like Claude or Gemini, with the modular design allowing easy extension of new automation skills.",
        "zh": "GenericAgent是一个轻量级Python框架，支持AI智能体通过浏览器和桌面自动化自主控制系统，降低传统智能体系统的计算成本。其核心采用自进化技能树架构，从3.3K行基础代码出发，通过高效记忆管理将令牌消耗降低6倍，平衡性能与效率。该框架适用于自动化测试、数据采集和工作流优化等场景，可集成Claude或Gemini等模型快速构建定制化智能体，模块化设计便于扩展新技能，提供灵活可靠的解决方案。",
        "es": "GenericAgent is a lightweight Python framework that enables AI agents to autonomously control computer systems through browser and desktop automation, solving the challenge of high computational costs in traditional agent systems. Its core innovation is a self-evolving skill tree that starts from a 3.3K-line seed and expands capabilities while reducing token consumption by 6x through efficient memory management. Developers can use it to build agents for tasks like automated testing, data collection, or workflow automation by integrating with models like Claude or Gemini, with the modular design allowing easy extension of new automation skills.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "GenericAgent stands out for ai-agent, automation, and autonomous-agent in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "GenericAgent is a lightweight Python framework that enables AI agents to autonomously control computer systems through browser and desktop automation, solving the challenge of high computational costs in traditional agent systems. Its core innovation is a self-evolving skill tree that starts from a 3.3K-line seed and expands capabilities while reducing token consumption by 6x through efficient memory management. Developers can use it to build agents for tasks like automated testing, data collection, or workflow automation by integrating with models like Claude or Gemini, with the modular design allowing easy extension of new automation skills.",
